WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.320
The Adventures of Sharkboy and Lavagirl in
3-D was essential viewing for many kids in

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.320
2005.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.890
The kid-friendly adventure film directed by
Robert Rodriguez follows the titular adolescent

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:13.400
superheroes as they come to life from the
imagination of a 10-year-old, bringing him

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.850
to their planet to protect it from aliens.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.630
Children who watched the movie in theaters
have likely been wondering what the heroes

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.789
have been up to for the last 15 years.

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:25.460
Now, they're about to get their answer, thanks
to Rodriguez's upcoming film We Can Be Heroes.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.279
The soon-to-be-released Netflix film primarily
focuses on a slightly different group of superheroes.

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:34.480
The likes of Marcus Moreno, played by Pedro
Pascal, and Christian Slater’s Tech-No,

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.270
make up a superhero collective known as the
Heroics.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.640
One day, the heroes are captured, and it's
up to their super-powered children to step

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.740
up and save the day.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.850
In the midst of this, Sharkboy and Lavagirl
return — now as adult heroes, who are married

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.300
and have a daughter of their own.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.330
Audiences with a penchant for thrillers may
actually recognize Sharkboy and Lavagirl's

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:55.610
daughter, who's known as Guppy; the actress
who plays her is Vivien Lyra Blair, who portrayed

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.320
Girl in the apocalyptic Netflix hit Bird Box.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.120
She'll be joined by the original Sharkgirl
star Taylor Dooley, who's returning as the

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.120
pink-haired heroine.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.119
To the disappointment of many, Taylor Lautner
will not be reprising his role for We Can

00:01:07.119 --> 00:01:11.409
Be Heroes, but based on photos released by
Netflix on Twitter, Sharkboy will still be

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:12.579
there, just played by J.J.

00:01:12.579 --> 00:01:14.079
Dashnaw this time around.

00:01:14.079 --> 00:01:17.340
And now, Sharkboy has the power to transform
into a giant glass shark.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:18.899
Talk about a glow-up!

00:01:18.899 --> 00:01:23.130
No word yet on whether Sharkboy goes by Sharkman
these days, but regardless, fans are hyped

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.509
to see the return of the two colorful characters.

00:01:25.509 --> 00:01:29.329
News of We Can Be Heroes coming to Netflix
has been out for a while now, as the project

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:31.810
was first announced in August 2019.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.679
Details were kept under wraps, but in a mid-November
2020 interview with Entertainment Weekly,

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:40.289
Rodriguez teased that We Can Be Heroes could
be considered a spiritual sequel of sorts

00:01:40.289 --> 00:01:42.950
to The Adventures of Sharkboy and Lavagirl
in 3-D.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.899
Just a few days later, Netflix confirmed that
We Can Be Heroes will indeed involve the two

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:49.640
vibrant heroes from many people's childhoods.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.069
While Sharkboy and Lavagirl won't be front
and center for the film, they'll be around

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:56.289
and have plenty of opportunities to show off
their respective powers.

00:01:56.289 --> 00:02:00.069
Hopefully their roles are more than just cameos,
because fans are ecstatic to relive their

00:02:00.069 --> 00:02:01.069
youth.

00:02:01.069 --> 00:02:02.319
Twitter user @antoinedaboi wrote,

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:05.849
"HOLY S--- 'WE CAN BE HEROES' WILL BE OUT
ON NEW YEARS...

00:02:05.849 --> 00:02:07.669
UGH CHILDHOOD IS COMING BACK."

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:08.700
Another fan tweeted,

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.239
"SHARKBOY AND LAVAGIRL IS BACK HOLY S--- MY
CHILDHOOD DREAMS ARE COMING TRUE."

00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:16.980
Netflix has a ton of content coming out in
the next couple of months, including a slew

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.980
of Christmas movies, but it's still understandable
if the only thing you can focus on now is

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:24.280
when you'll be able to watch a bunch of precocious
kids fight bad guys.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:28.840
For some, We Can Be Heroes takes precedence
over Oscar contenders, as evidenced by @TheDaddyKuma

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:29.840
saying,

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.661
"I can't see how anyone can care about Mank
when We Can Be Heroes is imminent, I just

00:02:33.661 --> 00:02:35.120
simply don't get it."

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.780
User @JabsSkyWalker agreed with that take,
tweeting,

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:41.700
"The Sharkboy and Lavagirl sequel will be
an Oscar nominated masterpiece."

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.830
One Twitter user had a more tempered reaction
to the news, though they did admit that they're,

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:49.730
quote, "super excited" to watch We Can Be
Heroes when it hits Netflix on January 1.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:50.730
They wrote,

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.980
"I absolutely adored Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.080
[...] I'm not expecting a cinematic masterpiece
or anything, but who knows.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.900
Maybe I'll be pleasantly surprised."

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.629
Though Sharkboy and Lavagirl's presence is
enough to get anyone excited, it's still unclear

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:03.549
what the extent of their roles will be.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:07.439
However, Twitter user @Edu_Alvarez1188 has
but one simple request,

00:03:07.439 --> 00:03:09.920
"We better get the Sharkboy Dream song [remastered]."

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.510
Going into 2021, that's probably all that
anyone really wants, at this point.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.560
And many are hoping that We Can Be Heroes
will be the saving grace of 2021.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.880
Twitterer @xenoworth wrote,

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:24.269
"if 2021 isn't good then at least we'll always
have the sharkboy and lavagirl sequel to fall

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:25.269
back on."

00:03:25.269 --> 00:03:26.790
While @VelocityPD_ wisely tweeted,

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:31.760
"if 2021 is starting with a sequel to Sharkboy
and Lavagirl then we might expect a good year."

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.650
You'll be able to see Sharkboy, Lavagirl,
and a bunch of new characters — like Priyanka

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:40.260
Chopra Jonas' Ms. Granada — suit up for
action when We Can Be Heroes drops on Netflix

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.739
on January 1, 2021.

